    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105-a3">

                <pb facs="0197" n="89" xml:id="pg89"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    117—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Diplomatic Corps to the Naval Commandants.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The diplomatic corps have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of the telegram of
                    the 13th of December, of the commanders of the foreign naval forces, and beg to
                    remark that they hold themselves, as they have heretofore, at their entire
                    disposal whenever imperative circumstances may render a conference necessary. A
                    notice, either by letter or telegram, sent in good time to Petropolis will
                    suffice to secure a meeting on the very next day at noon, at the dean of the
                    diplomatic corps, in the office of the British consulate, Travessa Dom Manoel,
                    No. 8, at Rio de Janeiro.</p>
            </div>
